      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Multisystem burden is a reasonable duration predictor. But the annual-physical row is labeled 'multiple_active_comorbidities' when the note describes a largely well patient (mild fatigue, single labs)—an unsupported assertion. Other samples (single_system, end_organ for post-MI) are sound. Notable overreach."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
  "source_groundedness": 0.8,
  "rationale": "The added columns collectively give strong, genuinely useful axes (interventions, workup scope, severity, referrals, counseling, comorbidity burden) directly relevant to predicting visit duration, well beyond generic length/sentiment flags. emergency_critical_status is near-constant in this sample and offers weaker leverage. Groundedness is generally good—silent rows correctly get 'not_present'—but several columns over-assert: 'medication_change' where regimens are continued, 'procedure_performed' for an ordered MRI, and 'multiple_active_comorbidities' for an essentially well patient. These recurring confident-specific inferences pull groundedness down modestly, though most values remain sound readings of the notes."
